YouHexen2 - music
=================

The original Hexen II PAK files contain MIDI music, but the HTML5 build has no MIDI synthesizer. Music in YouHexen2 therefore comes from external OGG Vorbis, MP3, FLAC, or WAV files imported through the PWA launcher.

The filename must match the MIDI name requested by the map, not the CD track number. For example, import casa1.ogg rather than track02.ogg. Loose music files are stored under data1/music/ by default; files already arranged under data1/music/ or portals/music/ retain those paths.

Hexen II:

  track02 -> casa1      track08 -> egyp3      track14 -> roma3
  track03 -> casa2      track09 -> meso1      track15 -> casb1
  track04 -> casa3      track10 -> meso2      track16 -> casb2
  track05 -> casa4      track11 -> meso3      track17 -> casb3
  track06 -> egyp1      track12 -> roma1
  track07 -> egyp2      track13 -> roma2

Portal of Praevus:

  track02 -> tulku7     track06 -> tulku9     track09 -> tulku5
  track03 -> tulku1     track07 -> tulku10    track10 -> tulku8
  track04 -> tulku4     track08 -> tulku6     track11 -> tulku3
  track05 -> tulku2

There is no track01 because the first track on the original discs is data. Portal track12 has no matching MIDI name.

To verify the build and a file, open the console with Shift+` and check for:

    BGM: MIDI driver: none (midi-named music will not play)
    BGM: stream codecs: ogg mp3 flac wav

Then run:

    music casa1

The bgm_remap command handles maps that request numeric CD tracks by pointing the request at a named file:

    bgm_remap 18 myambient
    bgm_remap list

See PWA.md for importing files and diagnosing silent music.
